--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/DYNAMIC_MAXIMUM.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Dynamic maximum: local derivative of MFGAdaUnlock-RenoDx 1.1
+
+This implementation only changes a successful, known-layout DWORD read of NVIDIA DRS key `0x10562D0F` for recognized Streamline/DLSSG consumers in this process. No DRS setters, global profile writes or NVAPI code patches are used. Existing Dynamic target, Fixed multiplier, MaxCount, latency and pacing logic remains upstream behavior.
+
+`DynamicMaxMultiplier=0` preserves NVIDIA behavior and installs no new GetProcAddress hook. Values 2 through 6 encode generated frames as value minus one. Invalid configuration preserves NVIDIA behavior. The effective value is frozen after LoadConfig, before compatibility/provider maintenance. UI changes apply after a full game restart.
+
+## ABI and consumer evidence
+
+The minimal V1 layout is independently expressed and checked with sizeof/offsetof assertions against [NVIDIA/nvapi commit 70d337db](https://github.com/NVIDIA/nvapi/tree/70d337db9186e968eab622f7e786de7e437faf3d): nvapi.h lines 24486–24521 and 25059–25076, nvapi_interface.h line 530, NvApiDriverSettings.h lines 728–734. V1 size is 0x3020, version 0x13020 and DWORD type is zero. Both input and output layout must match. A failure, including SETTING_NOT_FOUND, is always returned unchanged: the wrapper never fabricates a successful setting.
+
+[Streamline v2.14.1](https://github.com/NVIDIA-RTX/Streamline/tree/v2.14.1) `source/plugins/sl.common/drs.cpp` lines 86–123 and 154–158 implements application-only/current-profile reading followed by the separate caller fallback path. A successful overridden value is marked current-profile, while predefined metadata stays intact. Session or application-profile lookup failure happens before GetSetting and cannot be fixed by this wrapper.
+
+The supplied sl.common.dll (2.14.1.0, SHA256 `82924A8954DD671E09351C5DE0EB87AD0EB25B944CC9F9AB955CA1D9950DE15D`) was only statically inspected. Its exported slGetPluginFunction RVA 0x42C20 compares slSetTag at RVA 0x42C86 and returns 0x38BA0; slSetConstants at 0x42CC6 returns 0x39BA0; slEvaluateFeature at 0x42CE6 returns 0x3A0C0. These are actual in-module role endpoints, not an assumption about interposer exports. Public commonEntry.cpp lines 1982–1994 corroborate the gateway roles. Gateways are queried only; plugin load/start functions are never invoked by recognition.
+
+The supplied sl.dlss_g.dll (SHA256 `F4A6B2B14DCC0B1485989E430D3B4E3A44AC1800B92BA1AD74F476E64FB2B09C`) reads the key at RVA 0x41C56, tries DRSContext+0x20 at 0x41750, falls back to +0 at 0x41822, stores a nonzero result at configuration offset 0x2C, and forwards it to DLSSG.DynamicMaxFrameCount at 0x60EAC. Public source does not include this plugin implementation; these are binary observations, not claimed public implementation lines.
+
+sl.common caches GetSetting at RVA 0xC4B30: the stub checks it at 0x251F and resolves/caches QI 0x73BF8338 at 0x2537–0x2541. A getter cached before our hook is not repaired. The addon arms as early as its configuration permits and warns about already mapped Streamline; early loading still requires actual game verification. Consumers are checked at GetProcAddress, QI and getter use. A generic plugin gateway is insufficient. Renamed common/DLSSG modules must return the complete expected role set from their own module. Unknown future modules fail closed. Role recognition is compatibility scoping, not cryptographic code attestation.
+
+## Local tests
+
+- `dynamicmax_policy_tests.cpp`: 49 assertions passed using native C++ (ABI, caps, malformed config, metadata, failures).
+- `dynamicmax_hook_tests.cpp` with `dynamicmax_fixtures`: 21 assertions passed under MSVC C++20 /MT /O2 with the actual production Detours GetProcAddress hook, production recognizer and wrappers.
+- Fixtures cover first-query capture and caching, late-arm limitation, renamed common and DLSSG, unrelated and forwarded roles, borrowed QI/getter caller rejection, unknown ABI, unrelated keys, all tested real-getter errors, frozen configuration and cached callbacks after disarm.
+- The executable exports a minimal ReShade logging sink and loads only self-built inert DLLs, including an isolated nvapi64.dll fixture. No actual NVAPI/game DLL was executed.
+
+Build the fixture DLL with `nvapi_fixture.cpp` as nvapi64.dll; compile consumer_fixture.cpp with FIXTURE_ROLE=1 as early-common.dll and a19b836f.bin, role=0 as unrelated.dll, role=3 as forwarded.dll, role=2 as dlssg-role.bin. Compile dynamicmax_hook_tests.cpp with Detours and ReShade includes, link static detours.lib and user32.lib. Pass this isolated output directory as its sole argument. Use `tests/run_dynamicmax_tests.ps1 -DependencyDirectory <prepared-renodx-root> -OutputDirectory <new-empty-directory>` to build and run both suites. The dependency root must already contain external/Detours (built x64 static library and headers) and external/reshade headers. The script discovers MSVC using vswhere, or accepts -VcVarsAll, and saves build.cmd and build-test.log in the output directory. It does not download dependencies.
+
+Driver compatibility, interception armed, successful overridden read and actual gameplay ceiling are separate observations. No game/driver runtime ceiling is claimed by these tests. Getter failure, earlier caches, future ABI or pre-getter profile failure preserve NVIDIA defaults.
